<p>Ratings depend on model, length, and motor size. Use the supplier's load chart. See the <a href="/resources/conveyor-cost-guide/">conveyor cost guide</a> for pricing factors.</p>
<h2 id="apps-heading">Belt Conveyor Applications</h2>
<p><strong>Small product packaging:</strong> Slider bed belt conveyors with knife-edge transfers handle small products, bottles, pouches, cartons, blister packs, between filling, labeling, and case packing. The continuous belt surface supports products too small for <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/">roller conveyors</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Inspection and scanning:</strong> Belt conveyors provide a stable, flat surface for machine vision inspection, barcode scanning, and checkweighing. Products travel at consistent speed on the belt without vibration or rotation. The belt surface color (white, black, blue) contrasts with the product for vision system accuracy. Belt speed synchronizes with camera frame rates for sharp image capture.</p>
<p><strong>Incline and decline transport:</strong> Belt conveyors handle inclines that roller conveyors cannot (products slide backward on inclined rollers). Rough-top belts carry cases up inclines between floor levels. Cleated belts carry loose items up steeper inclines. Incline belt conveyors connect ground-level processes to mezzanines, <a href="/conveyor-types/spiral-conveyors/">spiral conveyors</a>, and <a href="/conveyor-types/diverting-merging/sortation/">sortation system</a> infeeds.</p>
<p><strong>Sortation induction:</strong> Belt conveyors with servo drives create precise product spacing (gapping) for sortation system induction. The belt accelerates each product to create a programmed gap between consecutive items. This gap ensures the <a href="/conveyor-types/diverting-merging/">sort mechanism</a> has time to reset between diverts. Induction belt speed is set by the sorter rate and product length.</p>
<p><strong><a href="/industries/food-conveyors/">Food processing and packaging:</a></strong> FDA-compliant belt conveyors handle direct food contact in bakery, confectionery, meat, and produce packaging. <a href="/industries/food-conveyors/sanitary/">Sanitary belt conveyors</a> use stainless steel frames, food-grade belting (polyurethane, silicone, or modular plastic), and tool-free belt release for cleaning and inspection.</p>
<p><strong><a href="/conveyor-types/accumulation-conveyors/">Zone accumulation:</a></strong> Servo-driven zone belt conveyors provide accumulation for products that cannot ride on rollers. Each belt zone operates independently with its own drive, providing zero-pressure accumulation for irregular shapes, polybags, and flexible packaging. Belt zone conveyors serve as an alternative to <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR roller conveyors</a> when the product demands a flat surface.</p>
